From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: fix MDIO bulk read buffer stride

The MDIO fallback stores each 32-bit register at val_buf + i, where
val_buf is a void pointer. Successive stores overlap by three bytes
and leave trailing output words unwritten. Advance in u32 units,
as the register loop and bulk write path already do.

QCA8386 uses this fallback for all switch accesses. A read-only
runtime comparison of three port status registers returned success
but disagreed with all three scalar reads, with the final bulk word
left at its initialized sentinel. FDB reads also use this bulk path.
This fixes a demonstrated data corruption bug; whether it contributes
to the separately observed shared egress stall requires traffic tests.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -630,7 +630,7 @@ qca8k_bulk_read(void *ctx, const void *r
 
 	/* loop count times and increment reg of 4 */
 	for (i = 0; i < count; i++, reg += sizeof(u32)) {
-		ret = qca8k_read_mii(priv, reg, val_buf + i);
+		ret = qca8k_read_mii(priv, reg, (u32 *)val_buf + i);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
 	}
